  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening sciences, technology, innovation, and engineering in East Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">African governments recognize that realizing the continent&apos;s socio-economic potential necessitates a comprehensive approach that leverages science, engineering, technology, and innovation to catalyze transformative change and add value to its abundant natural resources and demographic dividend of youth. African countries are actively embracing digital transformation, wherein the integration of digital technologies into the workforce and the emergence of innovative forms of entrepreneurship not only reshape job profiles but also offer novel solutions to social and economic challenges. This project aims at fortifying institutional and human capacities in basic science, research, and engineering to propel sustainable development in Eastern Africa.</narrative>
  </description>
